[sub_resource type="RectangleShape2D" id="RectangleShape2D_kill"]
size = Vector2(8000, 40)

; A mine head with two lifts and a roof under a chute (issue #143: #18's
; MovingPlatform used as lifts, plus #53's FallingRock). The high ground is
; worth taking, but it is always under fire.
;
; **Ground.** Two yards (x=+-300..+-740, top y=320) with a 600 px open pit
; between them. All eight spawns are in the yards. Their outer ends are open
; sky.
;
; **Lifts.** Each side of the pit has a lift (160 wide, x=+-100..+-260). It
; runs between flush with the yards (top y=320) and the roof's height (top
; y=-100) in 3 s each way. The two lifts run in opposite phase, so one is
; always at the bottom. The gap from a yard to a lift is 40 px, so you can
; step on at the bottom. If you miss it, you fall into the pit.
;
; **Roof.** A fixed slab (x=-90..90, top y=-122) between the tops of the two
; lifts' runs, 22 px above a lift at the top. It holds the best pickup. A
; FallingRock above it (the chute) drops onto the roof every 6 s after a
; 1.5 s warning. The rock knocks whoever holds the roof sideways, off a
; 180 px slab and 540 px above the pit.

; Backdrop (issue #117): dusty ochre dusk over spoil heaps.
